        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n2\n2 1\n3\n2 3 1\n5\n3 1 5 4 2\n6\n2 1 3 4 6 5\n4\n1 2 3 4",
        "output": "3\n5\n0\n3\n10",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 1 : The permutation P=[2,1]P = [2, 1]P=[2,1] is both 111-sortable and 222-sortable.\n\nK=1K = 1K=1 : Choose subset = [2][2][2], and add KKK to the 2nd2^{nd}2nd position, PPP becomes [2,2][2, 2][2,2].\nK=2K = 2K=2 : Choose subset = [2][2][2], and add KKK to the 2nd2^{nd}2nd position, PPP becomes [2,3][2, 3][2,3]."
      }
